{:edb/db-before-t 446 :edb/db-after-t 447 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533759 50 #inst "2026-10-04T20:07:08.771Z" 13194139533759 true] [17592186096539 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249776 13194139533759 true] [17592186096539 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249783 13194139533759 true] [17592186096539 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249787 13194139533759 true] [17592186096540 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249790 13194139533759 true] [17592186096540 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249797 13194139533759 true] [17592186249776 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249777 13194139533759 true] [17592186249776 1089 "q-11841" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249776 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533759 true] [17592186249776 1100 "Given that $f(x)=x\\cdot {3}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249776 1113 #uuid "c180c9d9-776e-5095-b2ca-7bd71cf574a7" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249776 1145 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)={3}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}\\cdot {3}^{x}+x\\cdot ({3}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & ={3}^{x}+(x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x}) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x} \\\\  & =(1+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249778 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249779 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249780 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249781 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249782 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1041 "selection" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249780 13194139533759 true] [17592186249777 1110 #uuid "fcb13a5f-9e2a-52d0-9caf-b5218e365c14" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249778 1034 "{3}^{x}" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249778 1111 #uuid "5d6ccc1e-c212-5844-b4ba-20c7d99f3135" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249779 1034 "(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249779 1111 #uuid "957cc015-2ff4-5858-80ca-542fc92725fc" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249780 1034 "(1+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249780 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249780 1111 #uuid "74e19656-27ba-5d17-ac41-eefac97766b9" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249781 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x}" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249781 1111 #uuid "a306448d-60e8-514b-9415-9e962562b712" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249782 1034 "(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249782 1111 #uuid "d23a480e-88a4-5af8-8779-11add69e1de0" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249783 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249784 13194139533759 true] [17592186249783 1089 "q-320814" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249783 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533759 true] [17592186249783 1100 "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}{log}_{3}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{{3}^{x}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249783 1113 #uuid "6755afd0-1d15-5a55-b5fd-7034b536b6e7" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249783 1145 "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)={log}_{3}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({3}^{x})}^{′}{log}_{3}⁡(x)+{3}^{x}{({log}_{3}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))({log}_{3}⁡(x))+({3}^{x})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3){log}_{3}⁡(x)+\\frac{{3}^{x}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249784 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249785 13194139533759 true] [17592186249784 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249786 13194139533759 true] [17592186249784 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533759 true] [17592186249784 1041 "field-1" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249784 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249786 13194139533759 true] [17592186249784 1110 #uuid "63e29222-5a8d-5853-8b80-3d161379b88e" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249785 1034 "3^x" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249785 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249785 1111 #uuid "6be1c15a-c1af-586e-ac41-5befb758f0ac" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249786 1034 "3^x\\ln(x)" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249786 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249786 1111 #uuid "5e3624fd-6a11-594f-901b-9f6c169c6684" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249787 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249788 13194139533759 true] [17592186249787 1089 "q-320815" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249787 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533759 true] [17592186249787 1100 "Given that $f(x)={4}^{x}{log}_{4}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={4}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4){log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249787 1113 #uuid "698df9b7-5456-5bcc-9e90-ffc1581df963" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249787 1145 "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={4}^{x}$ and $v(x)={log}_{4}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({4}^{x})}^{′}{log}_{4}⁡(x)+{4}^{x}{({log}_{4}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({4}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4))({log}_{4}⁡(x))+({4}^{x})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}) \\\\  & ={4}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4){log}_{4}⁡(x)+\\frac{{4}^{x}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249788 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249789 13194139533759 true] [17592186249788 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533759 true] [17592186249788 1041 "field-1" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249788 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249789 13194139533759 true] [17592186249788 1110 #uuid "1e915aa4-1cf3-58c6-a7f5-6d6f8030abff" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249789 1034 "\\frac{4^x}{x\\ln(4)}" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249789 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249789 1111 #uuid "5f494c67-2b1f-563c-b6ae-d467104f00fc" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249790 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249791 13194139533759 true] [17592186249790 1089 "q-48515" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249790 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533759 true] [17592186249790 1100 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(3x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=1.$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249790 1113 #uuid "330ecc2e-b308-5509-8b53-ac52f3ee0861" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249790 1145 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=3x-2$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(3x-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3x-2}{x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=1$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{3x-2}{x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1)-2}{1}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $1.$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249792 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249793 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249794 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249795 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249796 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1041 "selection" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249794 13194139533759 true] [17592186249791 1110 #uuid "b86965d0-31f0-5589-bffd-4b2285f7500f" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249792 1034 "1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249792 1111 #uuid "6dccbd62-8a05-598c-af35-b8e680f9de0a" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249793 1034 "5+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249793 1111 #uuid "551ef613-a012-5a64-a847-250d4db04faa" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249794 1034 "1" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249794 1111 #uuid "9d57a49d-f4ed-5d1c-9403-fa134933df8d" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249795 1034 "-4" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249795 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249795 1111 #uuid "912d0c11-5ebd-54e9-af91-d3d9997f436a" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249796 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249796 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249796 1111 #uuid "28f93fdb-a8a1-5944-8984-c11cadf0893d" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249797 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249798 13194139533759 true] [17592186249797 1089 "q-48517" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249797 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533759 true] [17592186249797 1100 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=({x}^{3}-1){e}^{x},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=2.$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249797 1113 #uuid "7d7f0345-c801-53f1-91dc-0c2acb65defb" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249797 1145 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{3}-1$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =({x}^{3}-1)\\cdot {e}^{x}+{e}^{x}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=2$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={{e}^{x}({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1)|}_{x=2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}({2}^{3}+3(2)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =19{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $19{e}^{2}.$" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249799 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249800 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249801 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249802 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249803 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1041 "selection" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249799 13194139533759 true] [17592186249798 1110 #uuid "179223e6-5b62-580e-9a38-cf433b22d31f" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249799 1034 "19{e}^{2}" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249799 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249799 1111 #uuid "347b555f-2854-5399-bcd2-629dddb1f8ab" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249800 1034 "4e" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249800 1111 #uuid "1aadf521-2119-50b9-be22-d834aac58344" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249801 1034 "{e}^{2}-1" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249801 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249801 1111 #uuid "e954f233-43ea-5227-838b-84aa28674fcb" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249802 1034 "3e+5" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533759 true] [17592186249802 1111 #uuid "1217113f-c35a-59ef-98ba-c0ec7ba67b9c" 13194139533759 true] [17592186249803 1034 "{e}^{2}+2" 13194139533759 tr